<title>PORTUGAL: U.S., Filipino firms bid for Portuguese carbon co.</title>
<headline>U.S., Filipino firms bid for Portuguese carbon co.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. firm Continental Carbon Company and Filipino company Indo Phil Textile Mills, Inc bid for Carbogal -- Carbonos de Portugal S.A., a unit of Portuguese state oil company Petroleos de Portugal S.A., Petrogal said.</p>
<p>Carbogal, which has a capital of 4.6 billion escudos, produces carbon black, a raw material used to make tyres.</p>
<p>Petrogal was selling 4.48 million series A and B shares, representing 97.36 percent of Carbogal.</p>
<p>The minimum bid must be 3.2 billion escudos.</p>
<p>The deadline for bids closed today at 1500 GMT. It was not immediately known when the winning bidder would be chosen.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
